    {
      "id": "te55",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 20,
      "y": 1095,
      "width": 1594.88,
      "height": 100.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 126603649,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 468597630,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Zone 0 is hostile: agent code, tool arguments and prose are all untrusted input to the runtime. The agent can never sign a receipt\nZone 1 is the only place execution is asserted, to the extent the TEE assumption holds and no further. If it is compromised, well-formed receipts about fictional execution verify\nZone 2 is trusted for availability and policy, not for evidence. It is a party, not a neutral oracle: it runs validators at v1 and its own stake is slashable\nZone 3 holds commitments, stake, escrow and verdicts, never task content. Dispute windows run on chain time, so the control plane cannot lengthen or shorten one\nD8: who may change the accepted-measurement list is a governance decision, because it decides which runtimes count",
      "originalText": "Zone 0 is hostile: agent code, tool arguments and prose are all untrusted input to the runtime. The agent can never sign a receipt\nZone 1 is the only place execution is asserted, to the extent the TEE assumption holds and no further. If it is compromised, well-formed receipts about fictional execution verify\nZone 2 is trusted for availability and policy, not for evidence. It is a party, not a neutral oracle: it runs validators at v1 and its own stake is slashable\nZone 3 holds commitments, stake, escrow and verdicts, never task content. Dispute windows run on chain time, so the control plane cannot lengthen or shorten one\nD8: who may change the accepted-measurement list is a governance decision, because it decides which runtimes count",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "te56",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 20,
      "y": 1209.0,
      "width": 1318.8000000000002,
      "height": 18.75,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#868e96",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1649767777,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 617255373,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Dashed arrows = public or attested paths \u00b7 Tags: OPEN = undecided (HLD section 11) \u00b7 Key custody design is a P1 and P2 deliverable \u00b7 Nothing here is measured",
      "originalText": "Dashed arrows = public or attested paths \u00b7 Tags: OPEN = undecided (HLD section 11) \u00b7 Key custody design is a P1 and P2 deliverable \u00b7 Nothing here is measured",
      "fontSize": 15,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
